Returns the address of the specified function for the current context. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function returns the address of the specified OpenGL or OpenGL ES core or extension function, if it is supported by the current context.\par
A context must be current on the calling thread. Calling this function without a current context will cause a {\b GLFW_NO_CURRENT_CONTEXT} error.\par
This function does not apply to Vulkan. If you are rendering with Vulkan, see glfwGetInstanceProcAddress, {\f2 vkGetInstanceProcAddr}  and {\f2 vkGetDeviceProcAddr}  instead.\par
